WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:03.471
- I've always been an
admirer of animation.

00:00:03.471 --> 00:00:07.598
It's an art form where
literally anything is possible.

00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:09.894
(pensive music)

00:00:09.894 --> 00:00:11.855
As someone who is on the autism spectrum,

00:00:11.855 --> 00:00:14.775
there are certain things
that I struggle with.

00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:18.733
I figured that working
in the field that I have

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:22.900
so much love for was nothing
more than like a pipe dream.

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:27.158
To feel like I've been
given this opportunity

00:00:27.158 --> 00:00:31.241
to prove myself, it's such
a amazing experience.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.047
My name is David Miles.

00:00:34.047 --> 00:00:37.016
I'm a junior VFX artist and animator

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:39.260
here at Exceptional Minds.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.055
- This is gonna be a
great class, you guys.

00:00:42.055 --> 00:00:43.507
And look around, these
are gonna be the people

00:00:43.507 --> 00:00:45.808
you're gonna work with
for a long time, too.

00:00:45.808 --> 00:00:47.345
Exceptional Minds is this amazing school

00:00:47.345 --> 00:00:49.264
for young adults on the autism spectrum.

00:00:49.264 --> 00:00:52.104
We teach them visual
effects and animation.

00:00:52.104 --> 00:00:53.991
Students go through a three-year program

00:00:53.991 --> 00:00:55.696
where they learn the basics of animation

00:00:55.696 --> 00:00:57.567
and visual effects, and then they learn

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:58.900
compositing and editing, so that they know

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.320
how to tell a story.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.946
The vast majority of
people with autism have

00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:05.033
extreme trouble finding work.

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.746
We're trying to create a place where

00:01:06.746 --> 00:01:08.868
people can take advantage
of their talents,

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.368
and they can reach great heights.

00:01:11.368 --> 00:01:14.042
- This is an animation project I did

00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:17.122
in my first year, made entirely in Flash.

00:01:17.122 --> 00:01:19.672
I'm gonna be starting an
internship at Cartoon Network,

00:01:19.672 --> 00:01:22.227
which I'm incredibly excited about.

00:01:22.227 --> 00:01:24.141
Knowing that I can make
a career out of this

00:01:24.141 --> 00:01:26.886
is probably one of the biggest reliefs,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:31.053
one of the best feelings
that I have ever experienced.

00:01:33.896 --> 00:01:38.023
One of the things I've discovered
being around other people

00:01:38.023 --> 00:01:42.151
who are on the autism
spectrum is that there is such

00:01:42.151 --> 00:01:46.951
a great variety of personality,
of creative potential.

00:01:46.951 --> 00:01:50.371
I've seen people who can
do absolutely mind-blowing

00:01:50.371 --> 00:01:53.206
things with special
effects, with animation.

00:01:53.206 --> 00:01:56.840
There is a certain advantage
to being able to think

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.257
very differently from the typical person.

00:02:04.798 --> 00:02:07.631
(electronic ping)

